solution.p:
With the expression 24\div(15\div 3+1) +2\text{,} well simplify whats inside the parentheses according to the order of operations, and then take 24 divided by that expression as our last step:
\begin{aligned}
24\div(15\div 3+1) +2\amp= 24\div(\nextoperation{15\div 3}+1) +2\\
\amp=24\div(\nextoperation{\highlight{5}+1}) +2\\
\amp=\nextoperation{24\div \highlight{6}}+2\\
\amp=\highlight{4}+2\\
\amp=\highlight{6}
\end{aligned}

